+# Cloudflare setup (generated, do not edit by hand)
+
+Generated by `scripts/generateCloudflareRules.ts` from `src/data/legacyRedirects.ts`.
+Goal: real HTTP 301 redirects and security/cache headers in front of GitHub Pages (audit items T-01, T-02).
+
+## 0. Put the site behind Cloudflare
+1. Add `easygradetool.com` to a free Cloudflare account and change the nameservers at your registrar.
+2. DNS: keep the records GitHub Pages needs (CNAME `www` → `<your-user>.github.io`, plus the four GitHub apex A records if you use the apex). Set the `www` record to **Proxied** (orange cloud).
+3. SSL/TLS mode: **Full** (GitHub Pages serves a valid certificate). Turn on **Always Use HTTPS**.
+4. Keep the existing `CNAME` file in the repo.
+
+## 1. Redirect Rules (Rules → Redirect Rules → Create rule)
+15 rules, grouped by target. If your Cloudflare plan allows fewer redirect rules than this, use Bulk Redirects (one list entry per legacy URL) instead; check the current limit in the dashboard.
+The 32 stub pages stay in the build as a fallback; once these rules are live, crawlers get a true 301 first.
+
+### Rule 1 → `/final-exam-grade-calculator/`
+
+Expression (Edit expression):
+```
+(http.host eq "www.easygradetool.com" and http.request.uri.path in {"/easy-grade-calculator/final-exam-grade-calculator" "/easy-grade-calculator/final-exam-grade-calculator/" "/easy-grade-calculator/college-final-grade-calculator" "/easy-grade-calculator/college-final-grade-calculator/" "/final-grade" "/final-grade/" "/final-grade-calculator" "/final-grade-calculator/"})
+```
+Then: **Static** redirect to `https://www.easygradetool.com/final-exam-grade-calculator/`, status **301**, preserve query string **on**.
+
